First, determine the location of the second stop. The trip was 60 miles long, and the second stop was 15 miles before the end, so the second stop was at 60 - 15 = 45 miles from the start.
Next, find the distance between the first and second stops. The first stop was at 20 miles, and the second stop was at 45 miles, so the distance between them was 45 - 20 = 25 miles.

\boxed{25}

38

The problem states that Grandma Jones baked 5 apple pies, and each pie was cut into 8 pieces. This means the total number of pieces of pie was 5 pies * 8 pieces/pie = 40 pieces. At the end of the evening, there were 14 pieces of pie remaining. Therefore, to find out how many pieces were taken by the guests, we subtract the remaining pieces from the total number of pieces: 40 pieces - 14 pieces = 26 pieces.

\boxed{26}

First, we determine the number of friends Amy made. Amy made 20 more friends than Lily, and Lily made 50 friends. Therefore, Amy made 50 + 20 = 70 friends.

Next, we find the total number of friends Lily and Amy have together. Lily has 50 friends and Amy has 70 friends, so together they have 50 + 70 = 120 friends.

\boxed{120}
